{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 42, :comments ["<b>And the fear of Yitzchak was for me.</b> Had it not been for the fear that you feared my father Yitzchak, that he is wealthy and a great prince." "<b>Was for me.</b> Its meaning: it was for me as help, for through this she (Rachel) was afraid. Another interpretation: the fear of Yitzchak toward HaShem was for me and helped me. Here Rashi commented: he did not wish to say 'Elohei Yitzchak' etc. It is difficult: see that Eliezer mentioned the special Name four times on behalf of Avraham." "<b>For now you would have sent me away empty.</b> To take my labor for nothing, as you wished."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {1 "Resolved ד״א as דבר אחר, 'another interpretation'; חז״ק as הכי קשיא, 'this is difficult'; abbreviation שע״י as שעל ידי, 'for through.'"}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:06:58.753652161Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}